  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bishops&apos; Ecumenical Pastoral Study Days</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support the running costs of an ecumenical course for pastoral reflection and analysis in Brazil.  

For many years a number of bishops and priests, of various religious denominations, from Brazil and several other Latin American countries have met annually to co-ordinate their work, provide mutual support and strengthen their action in favour of a preferential option for the poor.  

Since 1991 the planning, monitoring and follow up to the meetings has been organised with the support of CESEEP, an ecumenical training and research centre in Sao Paulo and long standing CAFOD partner (GLA045).  CAFOD has supported the course with small grants since 1991.  Each year the meeting is organised around a theme where the Church has a pastoral responsibility to give clear understanding and guidance.</narrative>
  </description>
